Messages⠀/⠀Chat⠀Transcript\n\nPresent⠀the⠀exchange⠀through⠀readable⠀sender-attributed⠀messages.⠀Include⠀only⠀the⠀timestamps,⠀delays,⠀edits,⠀receipts,⠀attachments,⠀or⠀channel⠀changes⠀that⠀matter⠀to⠀the⠀scene.⠀Let⠀each⠀person's⠀actual⠀digital⠀habits⠀shape⠀their⠀contribution:⠀one⠀may⠀write⠀in⠀full⠀sentences,⠀another⠀may⠀send⠀fragments,⠀a⠀third⠀may⠀leave⠀a⠀message⠀unsent.\n\nLet⠀wording,⠀a⠀remembered⠀phrase,⠀or⠀a⠀routine⠀request⠀meet⠀a⠀real⠀reply⠀or⠀pending⠀reception.⠀The⠀comic⠀relation⠀can⠀come⠀from⠀exact⠀fit,⠀calm⠀literal⠀understanding,⠀a⠀habitual⠀sign-off,⠀or⠀the⠀ordinary⠀timing⠀of⠀a⠀familiar⠀exchange.⠀Smooth⠀understanding⠀is⠀as⠀available⠀as⠀mismatch.⠀Do⠀not⠀invent⠀a⠀delay,⠀misread⠀receipt,⠀or⠀misunderstanding⠀to⠀create⠀subtext.\n\nPreserve⠀prior⠀knowledge,⠀drafts,⠀and⠀supported⠀access⠀through⠀other⠀means.⠀A⠀sent⠀message⠀is⠀distinct⠀from⠀an⠀unsent⠀draft,⠀and⠀private⠀thought⠀is⠀distinct⠀from⠀transmitted⠀text.⠀No⠀thought⠀is⠀automatically⠀transmitted.⠀If⠀the⠀active⠀contract⠀permits,⠀present⠀full⠀private⠀experience⠀outside⠀the⠀channel⠀in⠀clearly⠀separated⠀prose;⠀it⠀is⠀not⠀something⠀the⠀recipient⠀can⠀read.\n\nThe⠀boundary⠀may⠀arrive⠀before⠀composing,⠀sending,⠀or⠀receiving⠀is⠀complete.⠀The⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀a⠀message⠀half-written,⠀a⠀reply⠀pending,⠀or⠀a⠀sender⠀still⠀deciding⠀what⠀to⠀type.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPacaxba::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Comedy⠀/⠀Stephen⠀King⠀/⠀Visual⠀Novel\n\nOrient⠀the⠀scene⠀with⠀concise⠀setting,⠀readable⠀dialogue⠀attribution,⠀and⠀focal⠀narration⠀or⠀inner⠀response⠀in⠀a⠀rhythm⠀suited⠀to⠀an⠀illustrated⠀scene.⠀Establish⠀the⠀immediate⠀location⠀and⠀who⠀is⠀present⠀without⠀over-describing.⠀Let⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀attention⠀select⠀what⠀matters.\n\nA⠀supported⠀object⠀or⠀expression⠀cue⠀may⠀connect⠀a⠀known⠀routine⠀or⠀recollection⠀to⠀its⠀current⠀use.⠀The⠀cue⠀can⠀be⠀a⠀familiar⠀tool,⠀a⠀particular⠀look,⠀or⠀a⠀repeated⠀gesture.⠀Show⠀what⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀does⠀with⠀that⠀connection:⠀they⠀may⠀understand⠀the⠀relation,⠀misread⠀it,⠀or⠀miss⠀it⠀entirely.⠀The⠀cue⠀anchors⠀attentio