            "identifier": "nemo-init-recipes-crime-03",
            "name": "🔧 Init · Crime · 03/07",
            "content": "{{#if {{.NCGenreId == crime}}}}{{// @category Variable-Init }}{{// @icon 🔧 }}{{// @badge INIT }}{{// @tooltip Crime. Selected-partition data; keep enabled in supplied order after recipe selectors and before the Writing Recipe resolver. Part 3 of 7. }}{{// Source group: recipes-crime; payload preserved. }}{{setvar::NPadajan::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Light⠀Novel\n\nEnter⠀the⠀immediate⠀situation⠀cleanly.⠀Open⠀with⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀in⠀a⠀specific⠀place⠀and⠀time,⠀already⠀involved⠀in⠀the⠀crime's⠀preparation⠀or⠀aftermath:⠀waiting⠀in⠀a⠀car,⠀checking⠀a⠀bag,⠀walking⠀toward⠀a⠀meeting,⠀standing⠀in⠀a⠀room⠀where⠀something⠀has⠀just⠀happened.⠀Give⠀the⠀reader⠀the⠀essential⠀spatial⠀facts⠀in⠀the⠀first⠀few⠀lines:⠀where⠀the⠀character⠀is,⠀what⠀they⠀are⠀doing,⠀and⠀what⠀they⠀are⠀waiting⠀for⠀or⠀trying⠀to⠀avoid.\n\nKeep⠀spatial⠀changes⠀easy⠀to⠀follow.⠀When⠀the⠀character⠀moves⠀from⠀one⠀room⠀to⠀another,⠀from⠀a⠀street⠀to⠀a⠀building,⠀or⠀from⠀a⠀public⠀place⠀to⠀a⠀private⠀one,⠀mark⠀the⠀transition⠀with⠀a⠀concrete⠀detail:⠀a⠀door,⠀a⠀stairway,⠀a⠀change⠀in⠀light⠀or⠀sound.⠀Do⠀not⠀let⠀the⠀reader⠀lose⠀track⠀of⠀where⠀the⠀character⠀is⠀or⠀who⠀else⠀is⠀present.\n\nUse⠀readable⠀paragraph⠀breaks⠀around⠀action,⠀dialogue,⠀and⠀private⠀response.⠀Give⠀each⠀beat⠀its⠀own⠀space:⠀a⠀short⠀paragraph⠀for⠀a⠀physical⠀action,⠀a⠀separate⠀block⠀for⠀speech,⠀and⠀a⠀separate⠀block⠀for⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character's⠀reaction.⠀Keep⠀the⠀prose⠀fast⠀and⠀clear,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀reduce⠀every⠀paragraph⠀to⠀a⠀single⠀sentence.⠀Let⠀the⠀breaks⠀create⠀rhythm⠀without⠀fragmenting⠀the⠀scene.\n\nUse⠀Murakami's⠀calm,⠀even⠀attention⠀for⠀exact⠀surfaces.⠀Describe⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀a⠀bag,⠀the⠀time⠀on⠀a⠀phone,⠀the⠀position⠀of⠀a⠀hand,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀door⠀closing,⠀the⠀smell⠀of⠀rain⠀or⠀coffee.⠀Let⠀these⠀details⠀carry⠀the⠀tension.⠀A⠀threat⠀may⠀be⠀spoken⠀in⠀a⠀quiet⠀voice⠀while⠀someone⠀checks⠀a⠀message.⠀A⠀body⠀or⠀injury⠀may⠀be⠀described⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀plain⠀register⠀as⠀a⠀broken⠀appliance⠀or⠀a⠀missed⠀train.\n\nMake⠀the⠀crime⠀concrete⠀and⠀motivated.⠀The⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀may⠀be⠀preparing⠀to⠀steal,⠀deliver,⠀hide,⠀or⠀destroy⠀something;⠀they⠀may⠀be⠀meeting⠀an⠀accomplice,⠀avoiding⠀a⠀pursuer,⠀or⠀returning⠀to⠀a⠀place⠀where⠀an⠀offense⠀occurred.⠀Show⠀the⠀incentive⠀through⠀specific⠀actions⠀and⠀dialogue:⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀needs,⠀what⠀they⠀are⠀willing⠀to⠀risk,⠀what⠀they⠀will⠀not⠀say.⠀Do⠀not⠀summarize⠀the⠀crime⠀in⠀exposition;⠀let⠀it⠀emerge⠀through⠀the⠀scene.\n\nInclude⠀focused⠀reaction⠀beats⠀after⠀significant⠀actions⠀or⠀dialogue.⠀The⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀may⠀notice⠀a⠀detail,⠀feel⠀a⠀physical⠀sensation,⠀make⠀a⠀calculation,⠀or⠀recognize⠀that⠀a⠀situation⠀has⠀changed.⠀Keep⠀the⠀reaction⠀specific⠀and⠀owned⠀by⠀the⠀character:⠀a⠀tightening⠀in⠀the⠀chest,⠀a⠀decision⠀to⠀leave,⠀a⠀memory⠀that⠀surfaces,⠀a⠀question⠀they⠀decide⠀not⠀to⠀ask.⠀The⠀reaction⠀may⠀be⠀serious,⠀uncertain,⠀angry,⠀or⠀calm⠀according⠀to⠀the⠀character's⠀actual⠀state.\n\nLet⠀the⠀scene⠀end⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀continuation⠀point⠀without⠀requiring⠀a⠀cliffhanger.⠀The⠀response⠀may⠀stop⠀while⠀the⠀character⠀is⠀still⠀waiting,⠀still⠀walking,⠀still⠀deciding,⠀or⠀still⠀in⠀the⠀middle⠀of⠀a⠀conversation.⠀The⠀crime's⠀consequences⠀may⠀remain⠀unfinished.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀reversal,⠀confession,⠀or⠀completed⠀action⠀at⠀the⠀end⠀of⠀every⠀response.\n\nDo⠀not⠀require⠀first⠀person,⠀comedy,⠀a⠀young⠀cast,⠀or⠀a⠀closing⠀cliffhanger.⠀The⠀light⠀novel⠀container⠀supplies⠀fast-readable⠀staging⠀and⠀focused⠀reactions,⠀not⠀a⠀particular⠀tone⠀or⠀demographic.⠀Any⠀strangeness⠀remains⠀psychological⠀and⠀situational:⠀a⠀person⠀who⠀behaves⠀as⠀if⠀following⠀a⠀private⠀rule,⠀a⠀room⠀that⠀feels⠀different⠀after⠀an⠀argument,⠀a⠀coincidence⠀that⠀seems⠀to⠀confirm⠀a⠀private⠀fear.⠀Treat⠀such⠀strangeness⠀as⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀ordinary⠀world,⠀never⠀as⠀a⠀supernatural⠀explanation.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajao::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Lyrical⠀Prose\n\nLet⠀the⠀rhythm⠀of⠀a⠀paragraph⠀follow⠀the⠀way⠀attention⠀moves⠀through⠀a⠀scene:⠀from⠀an⠀exact⠀practical⠀surface⠀to⠀the⠀association⠀it⠀raises,⠀then⠀back⠀to⠀a⠀consequential⠀detail⠀of⠀the⠀offense⠀or⠀its⠀aftermath.⠀A⠀comparison⠀begins⠀in⠀something⠀actually⠀present—a⠀receipt⠀left⠀on⠀a⠀counter,⠀the⠀smell⠀of⠀cleaning⠀fluid,⠀the⠀way⠀a⠀door⠀closes⠀against⠀its⠀frame—and⠀unfolds⠀only⠀when⠀it⠀changes⠀what⠀the⠀narrator⠀understands⠀or⠀makes⠀a⠀private⠀concern⠀more⠀present.⠀Keep⠀the⠀crime's⠀causal⠀chain⠀legible⠀inside⠀the⠀imagery.⠀If⠀a⠀figure⠀of⠀speech⠀suggests⠀concealment,⠀pressure,⠀or⠀exposure,⠀let⠀a⠀later⠀concrete⠀fact⠀show⠀what⠀that⠀perception⠀means⠀rather⠀than⠀letting⠀the⠀comparison⠀stand⠀in⠀for⠀evidence.\n\nUse⠀recurring⠀sounds⠀and⠀images⠀as⠀an⠀organizing⠀device,⠀not⠀as⠀decoration.⠀A⠀repeated⠀image⠀returns⠀when⠀a⠀later⠀occurrence⠀gives⠀it⠀new⠀significance:⠀the⠀same⠀train⠀announcement⠀heard⠀before⠀a⠀meeting⠀and⠀after⠀a⠀confession,⠀the⠀same⠀color⠀noticed⠀on⠀a⠀coat⠀and⠀then⠀on⠀a⠀document.⠀The⠀repetition⠀deepens⠀the⠀reader's⠀sense⠀of⠀how⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀is⠀processing⠀events,⠀not⠀signal⠀that⠀the⠀image⠀itself⠀is⠀a⠀clue.⠀Plain⠀statements⠀interrupt⠀the⠀lyrical⠀movement⠀at⠀moments⠀of⠀practical⠀consequence,⠀so⠀that⠀an⠀arrest,⠀a⠀payment,⠀a⠀lie,⠀or⠀a⠀piece⠀of⠀damage⠀remains⠀direct⠀and⠀unmistakable.\n\nPreserve⠀the⠀narrator's⠀conversational⠀distance⠀even⠀when⠀the⠀prose⠀grows⠀associative.⠀The⠀teller⠀may⠀notice⠀that⠀an⠀ordinary⠀object⠀seems⠀to⠀hold⠀more⠀meaning⠀than⠀it⠀should,⠀but⠀the⠀narration⠀does⠀not⠀claim⠀that⠀the⠀object⠀is⠀magical⠀or⠀that⠀the⠀world⠀has⠀become⠀unstable.⠀Keep⠀uncertainty⠀available⠀without⠀making⠀every⠀scene⠀fact⠀ambiguous.⠀A⠀character⠀can⠀feel⠀that⠀a⠀room⠀has⠀changed⠀after⠀a⠀crime⠀without⠀the⠀prose⠀asserting⠀that⠀the⠀room⠀literally⠀changed.⠀Let⠀the⠀account⠀end⠀where⠀the⠀selected⠀scene⠀ends,⠀with⠀the⠀crime's⠀consequences⠀still⠀developing⠀rather⠀than⠀resolved⠀into⠀a⠀lesson.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajap::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Melancholic⠀/⠀Reflective\n\nLet⠀the⠀crime's⠀aftermath⠀supply⠀the⠀specific⠀irreversible⠀changes⠀the⠀narration⠀reflects⠀on.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀notice⠀that⠀a⠀familiar⠀routine⠀continues⠀after⠀an⠀offense⠀but⠀no⠀longer⠀means⠀what⠀it⠀did:⠀the⠀same⠀shop⠀is⠀open,⠀the⠀same⠀train⠀arrives,⠀the⠀same⠀person⠀answers⠀the⠀phone,⠀yet⠀the⠀attention⠀now⠀moves⠀toward⠀what⠀has⠀become⠀unavailable.⠀Keep⠀the⠀reflection⠀anchored⠀to⠀the⠀actual⠀consequences⠀of⠀the⠀crime—a⠀missing⠀person,⠀a⠀broken⠀arrangement,⠀a⠀debt,⠀a⠀silence,⠀a⠀place⠀that⠀can⠀no⠀longer⠀be⠀entered⠀without⠀remembering.⠀Do⠀not⠀announce⠀that⠀everything⠀passes⠀or⠀that⠀loss⠀is⠀universal.⠀Let⠀one⠀particular⠀change⠀carry⠀the⠀feeling.\n\nUse⠀remembered⠀occasions⠀as⠀a⠀way⠀to⠀show⠀how⠀the⠀present⠀experience⠀coexists⠀with⠀what⠀is⠀gone.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀recall⠀a⠀conversation⠀while⠀performing⠀an⠀ordinary⠀task,⠀or⠀recognize⠀that⠀a⠀familiar⠀object⠀now⠀belongs⠀to⠀a⠀different⠀time.⠀The⠀memory⠀should⠀be⠀specific⠀enough⠀to⠀matter:⠀who⠀said⠀what,⠀where⠀the⠀light⠀fell,⠀what⠀was⠀left⠀unfinished.⠀Let⠀ordinary⠀pleasure⠀remain⠀available.⠀A⠀meal⠀can⠀still⠀be⠀good,⠀a⠀walk⠀can⠀still⠀be⠀pleasant,⠀a⠀joke⠀can⠀still⠀land,⠀even⠀while⠀the⠀character⠀carries⠀an⠀unresolved⠀attachment⠀or⠀an⠀unhealed⠀consequence.\n\nPreserve⠀Murakami's⠀conversational⠀distance.⠀The⠀narrator⠀may⠀reflect⠀directly,⠀but⠀the⠀reflection⠀should⠀sound⠀like⠀a⠀person⠀noticing⠀something⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀voice⠀delivering⠀an⠀elegy.⠀Keep⠀the⠀account⠀unhurried⠀without⠀drifting⠀away⠀from⠀the⠀crime.⠀When⠀a⠀practical⠀matter⠀intervenes—a⠀call,⠀a⠀payment,⠀a⠀question⠀from⠀someone⠀involved—let⠀it⠀interrupt⠀the⠀reflective⠀movement⠀naturally.⠀The⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀character⠀still⠀inside⠀the⠀aftermath,⠀neither⠀healed⠀nor⠀destroyed,⠀attending⠀to⠀the⠀next⠀small⠀thing.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajaq::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Middle⠀Eastern⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nUse⠀framed⠀oral⠀storytelling⠀as⠀the⠀concrete⠀regional⠀route.⠀Establish⠀a⠀situated⠀teller⠀and⠀a⠀listener⠀or⠀audience⠀whose⠀presence⠀shapes⠀the⠀account.⠀The⠀teller⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀bystander,⠀an⠀investigator,⠀a⠀neighbor,⠀or⠀someone⠀who⠀knew⠀the⠀people⠀involved,⠀but⠀the⠀telling⠀remains⠀a⠀composed⠀account⠀delivered⠀in⠀a⠀particular⠀time⠀and⠀place,⠀not⠀an⠀omniscient⠀chronicle.⠀Let⠀the⠀frame⠀return⠀at⠀intervals:⠀the⠀listener⠀asks⠀a⠀question,⠀the⠀teller⠀pauses⠀to⠀make⠀tea,⠀a⠀noise⠀from⠀the⠀street⠀interrupts,⠀or⠀the⠀teller⠀admits⠀uncertainty⠀about⠀a⠀detail.⠀These⠀returns⠀keep⠀the⠀crime's⠀account⠀grounded⠀in⠀the⠀relationship⠀between⠀teller⠀and⠀listener.\n\nPreserve⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀attention⠀inside⠀the⠀telling.⠀The⠀teller⠀describes⠀exact⠀surfaces—a⠀doorway,⠀a⠀receipt,⠀a⠀telephone,⠀the⠀way⠀someone⠀folded⠀a⠀coat—and⠀lets⠀ordinary⠀activities⠀carry⠀the⠀narrative⠀forward.⠀The⠀crime⠀emerges⠀through⠀preparation,⠀incentives,⠀relationships,⠀execution,⠀evidence,⠀or⠀aftermath⠀as⠀the⠀teller⠀relates⠀them.⠀Suspense⠀can⠀come⠀from⠀what⠀the⠀teller⠀chooses⠀to⠀delay,⠀repeat,⠀or⠀qualify,⠀even⠀when⠀the⠀listener⠀already⠀knows⠀the⠀outcome.⠀When⠀the⠀teller⠀repeats⠀a⠀phrase⠀or⠀returns⠀to⠀an⠀image,⠀the⠀repetition⠀marks⠀a⠀shift⠀in⠀understanding⠀or⠀emphasis,⠀not⠀ornament.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀regional⠀selection⠀distinct⠀without⠀importing⠀a⠀new⠀setting,⠀religion,⠀honor⠀code,⠀or⠀mystical⠀apparatus.⠀The⠀supplied⠀world⠀and⠀cast⠀remain⠀unchanged.⠀The⠀framed⠀telling⠀may⠀include⠀reflective⠀or⠀philosophical⠀passages,⠀but⠀they⠀arise⠀from⠀the⠀teller's⠀actual⠀situation⠀and⠀the⠀crime's⠀particular⠀consequences.⠀Let⠀the⠀teller⠀distinguish⠀what⠀they⠀saw⠀from⠀what⠀they⠀heard,⠀and⠀what⠀they⠀know⠀from⠀what⠀they⠀suppose.⠀The⠀account⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀the⠀frame⠀still⠀open—the⠀listener⠀preparing⠀to⠀leave,⠀the⠀teller⠀returning⠀to⠀a⠀task—rather⠀than⠀closing⠀with⠀a⠀moral⠀or⠀a⠀completed⠀judgment.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajar::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Minimalist⠀Prose\n\nSelect⠀a⠀small⠀number⠀of⠀exact⠀details⠀and⠀let⠀them⠀carry⠀the⠀scene's⠀weight.⠀One⠀detail⠀can⠀stand⠀for⠀a⠀larger⠀condition:⠀a⠀cup⠀left⠀unwashed,⠀a⠀phone⠀number⠀written⠀twice,⠀a⠀door⠀that⠀no⠀longer⠀locks.⠀Choose⠀details⠀that⠀belong⠀to⠀the⠀crime's⠀preparation,⠀execution,⠀or⠀aftermath,⠀and⠀let⠀them⠀remain⠀concrete⠀rather⠀than⠀explained.⠀The⠀narrator's⠀private⠀concern⠀appears⠀through⠀what⠀gets⠀noticed⠀and⠀what⠀gets⠀omitted,⠀not⠀through⠀a⠀paragraph⠀of⠀interpretation.⠀When⠀an⠀inward⠀connection⠀is⠀essential,⠀state⠀it⠀in⠀a⠀direct⠀clause⠀and⠀stop.\n\nKeep⠀clauses⠀short⠀and⠀movement⠀economical,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀delete⠀causality.⠀The⠀reader⠀should⠀be⠀able⠀to⠀infer⠀why⠀a⠀person⠀acts,⠀what⠀a⠀piece⠀of⠀evidence⠀implies,⠀or⠀how⠀a⠀relationship⠀has⠀changed.⠀If⠀a⠀step⠀in⠀the⠀crime's⠀logic⠀would⠀otherwise⠀disappear,⠀include⠀the⠀necessary⠀fact⠀or⠀action⠀in⠀plain⠀terms.⠀Omission⠀leaves⠀something⠀inferable,⠀not⠀a⠀gap⠀where⠀motivation⠀or⠀consequence⠀should⠀be.⠀A⠀precise⠀extended⠀sentence⠀is⠀acceptable⠀when⠀it⠀serves⠀the⠀account⠀better⠀than⠀several⠀fragmented⠀ones.\n\nPreserve⠀Murakami's⠀even⠀tone⠀and⠀conversational⠀distance⠀without⠀drifting⠀into⠀associative⠀expansion.⠀Strangeness⠀is⠀stated⠀evenly,⠀as⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀scene,⠀not⠀amplified.⠀Let⠀dialogue⠀remain⠀individual⠀and⠀economical.⠀The⠀account⠀can⠀end⠀after⠀a⠀single⠀consequential⠀action⠀or⠀observation,⠀with⠀the⠀next⠀development⠀left⠀unstated⠀but⠀inferable⠀from⠀what⠀has⠀been⠀established.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajas::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Modern⠀Literature⠀/⠀Contemporary⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀sustained⠀scene-first⠀prose⠀in⠀which⠀the⠀crime's⠀movement⠀is⠀carried⠀by⠀action,⠀dialogue,⠀perception,⠀recollection,⠀and⠀authorized⠀inner⠀experience.⠀Open⠀a⠀scene⠀in⠀a⠀concrete⠀present⠀moment—a⠀person⠀arriving⠀somewhere,⠀a⠀task⠀being⠀done,⠀a⠀conversation⠀beginning—and⠀let⠀the⠀narrative⠀move⠀naturally⠀among⠀what⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀sees,⠀says,⠀remembers,⠀and⠀privately⠀thinks.⠀Keep⠀transitions⠀unobtrusive.⠀A⠀recollection⠀can⠀arise⠀from⠀a⠀present⠀detail,⠀and⠀a⠀return⠀to⠀the⠀scene⠀can⠀be⠀marked⠀by⠀a⠀new⠀action⠀or⠀a⠀shift⠀in⠀attention⠀rather⠀than⠀a⠀summary.\n\nPreserve⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀activities⠀and⠀conversational⠀distance⠀within⠀the⠀novelistic⠀flow.⠀Let⠀ordinary⠀tasks⠀occupy⠀real⠀narrative⠀space:⠀preparing⠀food,⠀waiting⠀for⠀a⠀train,⠀sorting⠀papers,⠀walking⠀to⠀a⠀meeting.⠀These⠀activities⠀hold⠀the⠀reader's⠀attention⠀while⠀the⠀crime's⠀incentives,⠀relationships,⠀and⠀consequences⠀develop⠀around⠀them.⠀Strangeness⠀is⠀described⠀evenly,⠀as⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀scene's⠀texture,⠀without⠀the⠀narration⠀insisting⠀on⠀its⠀meaning.⠀The⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀may⠀associate⠀an⠀ordinary⠀object⠀with⠀a⠀private⠀concern,⠀but⠀the⠀prose⠀does⠀not⠀stop⠀to⠀explain⠀the⠀association⠀unless⠀the⠀explanation⠀contributes⠀to⠀the⠀present⠀account.\n\nLet⠀paragraphing⠀orient⠀the⠀reader⠀without⠀recap⠀machinery.⠀A⠀new⠀paragraph⠀marks⠀a⠀shift⠀in⠀speaker,⠀a⠀change⠀in⠀location,⠀a⠀movement⠀from⠀perception⠀to⠀thought,⠀or⠀a⠀development⠀in⠀the⠀crime's⠀progress.⠀Do⠀not⠀restate⠀what⠀the⠀reader⠀already⠀knows.⠀The⠀register⠀and⠀rhythm⠀follow⠀the⠀narrator's⠀voice⠀and⠀the⠀immediate⠀scene,⠀not⠀a⠀fixed⠀template.⠀The⠀scene⠀can⠀end⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀boundary—a⠀conversation⠀concluded,⠀a⠀task⠀interrupted,⠀a⠀decision⠀deferred—without⠀requiring⠀a⠀lesson,⠀a⠀reversal,⠀or⠀a⠀completed⠀development.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajat::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Relationship-Centric⠀Fanfiction⠀(AO3-inspired)\n\nMake⠀the⠀established⠀relationship⠀premise⠀the⠀organizing⠀lens⠀for⠀the⠀crime⠀story.⠀Select⠀scenes⠀that⠀show⠀how⠀the⠀offense,⠀scheme,⠀investigation,⠀or⠀aftermath⠀touches⠀the⠀relationship:⠀a⠀shared⠀errand⠀becomes⠀implicated,⠀a⠀private⠀joke⠀resurfaces⠀under⠀pressure,⠀a⠀moment⠀of⠀comfort⠀follows⠀a⠀disclosure,⠀a⠀divided⠀loyalty⠀makes⠀an⠀ordinary⠀conversation⠀difficult.⠀Let⠀the⠀relationship's⠀particular⠀promise⠀shape⠀what⠀gets⠀attention.⠀If⠀the⠀premise⠀is⠀built⠀on⠀trust,⠀show⠀what⠀trust⠀costs⠀under⠀suspicion;⠀if⠀it⠀is⠀built⠀on⠀rivalry,⠀show⠀how⠀the⠀crime⠀changes⠀the⠀terms⠀of⠀competition;⠀if⠀it⠀is⠀built⠀on⠀care,⠀show⠀care⠀continuing⠀even⠀when⠀circumstances⠀grow⠀dangerous.⠀Do⠀not⠀insert⠀a⠀roster⠀of⠀familiar⠀tropes.⠀Use⠀only⠀the⠀actual⠀supplied⠀premise.\n\nGive⠀private⠀language⠀and⠀repeated⠀moments⠀room⠀to⠀work.⠀A⠀phrase⠀the⠀characters⠀use⠀with⠀each⠀other⠀can⠀return⠀at⠀a⠀consequential⠀moment⠀and⠀mean⠀something⠀new.⠀A⠀small⠀ritual—a⠀way⠀of⠀greeting,⠀a⠀shared⠀meal,⠀a⠀particular⠀route⠀walked⠀together—becomes⠀the⠀site⠀where⠀the⠀crime's⠀pressure⠀becomes⠀visible.⠀Let⠀affection,⠀jealousy,⠀comfort,⠀rivalry,⠀or⠀discovery⠀occupy⠀real⠀narrative⠀space⠀rather⠀than⠀being⠀summarized.⠀Preserve⠀Murakami's⠀conversational⠀distance:⠀the⠀emotional⠀payoff⠀emerges⠀through⠀exact⠀surfaces⠀and⠀restrained⠀dialogue,⠀not⠀through⠀characters⠀announcing⠀their⠀feelings⠀in⠀polished⠀speeches.⠀The⠀narrator⠀may⠀observe⠀that⠀something⠀between⠀them⠀has⠀changed,⠀but⠀the⠀change⠀is⠀shown⠀in⠀what⠀they⠀do⠀and⠀say.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀crime's⠀causal⠀chain⠀intact.⠀The⠀relationship⠀is⠀not⠀a⠀substitute⠀for⠀evidence,⠀motive,⠀or⠀consequence.⠀Suspense⠀can⠀arise⠀from⠀exposure⠀or⠀divided⠀loyalty⠀even⠀when⠀the⠀reader⠀knows⠀who⠀did⠀it.⠀Let⠀the⠀scene⠀end⠀at⠀a⠀natural⠀relationship⠀boundary—a⠀reassurance⠀given,⠀a⠀question⠀left⠀unanswered,⠀a⠀door⠀closed,⠀a⠀hand⠀withdrawn—without⠀requiring⠀a⠀confession,⠀a⠀reconciliation,⠀or⠀a⠀completed⠀emotional⠀arc.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajau::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Saga⠀/⠀Oral⠀Epic\n\nGive⠀the⠀crime⠀account⠀the⠀sense⠀of⠀a⠀retelling.⠀Open⠀with⠀a⠀deliberate⠀declaration⠀that⠀establishes⠀the⠀offense⠀or⠀its⠀consequence⠀as⠀something⠀people⠀will⠀remember:⠀who⠀did⠀what,⠀who⠀was⠀there,⠀what⠀changed⠀afterward.⠀Then⠀expand⠀into⠀the⠀particulars⠀that⠀make⠀the⠀declaration⠀incomplete.⠀The⠀telling⠀relates⠀preparation,⠀incentives,⠀relationships,⠀execution,⠀evidence,⠀pursuit,⠀and⠀aftermath⠀as⠀deeds⠀whose⠀consequences⠀accumulate⠀over⠀time.⠀A⠀compact⠀declaration⠀can⠀introduce⠀a⠀person⠀or⠀an⠀act,⠀but⠀it⠀is⠀grounded⠀in⠀what⠀actually⠀happened,⠀not⠀inflated⠀into⠀legend.\n\nUse⠀recurring⠀phrasing⠀to⠀mark⠀the⠀account's⠀shape.⠀A⠀phrase⠀returns⠀when⠀a⠀later⠀occurrence⠀gives⠀it⠀a⠀new⠀application:⠀the⠀same⠀description⠀of⠀a⠀door,⠀a⠀debt,⠀a⠀silence,⠀or⠀a⠀promise,⠀repeated⠀after⠀the⠀crime⠀has⠀changed⠀what⠀it⠀means.⠀Let⠀the⠀recurrence⠀deepen⠀the⠀reader's⠀sense⠀of⠀consequence⠀rather⠀than⠀decorate⠀every⠀entrance.⠀Keep⠀the⠀teller's⠀access⠀consistent⠀with⠀the⠀selected⠀perspective.⠀The⠀account⠀may⠀relate⠀what⠀people⠀said⠀and⠀did,⠀but⠀it⠀does⠀not⠀claim⠀to⠀know⠀every⠀private⠀mind⠀unless⠀the⠀perspective⠀permits⠀it.\n\nPreserve⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀practical⠀attention⠀and⠀conversational⠀distance.⠀The⠀chronicle⠀remains⠀close⠀to⠀ordinary⠀surfaces:⠀who⠀lent⠀the⠀thing,⠀who⠀repaired⠀it,⠀who⠀waited,⠀who⠀answered⠀the⠀phone.⠀Strangeness⠀is⠀stated⠀evenly.⠀Let⠀dialogue⠀interrupt⠀the⠀authority⠀of⠀the⠀retelling⠀when⠀a⠀participant⠀objects⠀to⠀a⠀detail⠀or⠀answers⠀an⠀elevated⠀introduction⠀with⠀an⠀ordinary⠀practical⠀concern.⠀The⠀account⠀can⠀end⠀with⠀a⠀deed⠀concluded⠀or⠀resumed,⠀leaving⠀another⠀consequence⠀available⠀to⠀be⠀remembered⠀rather⠀than⠀declaring⠀the⠀crime⠀a⠀completed⠀legend.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajav::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Scandinavian⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nWrite⠀the⠀narrative⠀as⠀a⠀social-realist⠀account⠀of⠀an⠀offense⠀and⠀its⠀consequences,⠀anchored⠀in⠀a⠀concrete⠀Scandinavian⠀setting.⠀Choose⠀the⠀specific⠀institution⠀and⠀domestic⠀world⠀the⠀story⠀inhabits:⠀a⠀municipal⠀housing⠀office⠀and⠀its⠀waiting-room⠀routines;⠀a⠀workplace⠀union⠀representative⠀navigating⠀sick-leave⠀rules;⠀a⠀small-town⠀police⠀station⠀handling⠀a⠀reported⠀theft;⠀a⠀parent⠀coordinator⠀at⠀a⠀day-care⠀center;⠀a⠀social⠀worker⠀visiting⠀a⠀family⠀after⠀a⠀complaint.⠀Keep⠀the⠀setting⠀definite,⠀but⠀do⠀not⠀assume⠀snow,⠀isolation,⠀or⠀silence.\n\nUse⠀a⠀single⠀focal⠀viewpoint⠀from⠀the⠀crime's⠀orbit:⠀an⠀investigator,⠀a⠀neighbor,⠀a⠀relative,⠀a⠀victim,⠀or⠀someone⠀implicated.⠀Let⠀that⠀character's⠀practical⠀tasks⠀continue⠀around⠀the⠀offense.⠀Show⠀how⠀they⠀make⠀coffee,⠀wait⠀for⠀a⠀bus,⠀complete⠀a⠀form,⠀lock⠀a⠀door,⠀stack⠀boxes,⠀or⠀prepare⠀a⠀meal.⠀Describe⠀these⠀actions⠀with⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀exactness,⠀allowing⠀ordinary⠀domestic⠀and⠀bureaucratic⠀detail⠀to⠀carry⠀feeling⠀and⠀implication⠀without⠀commentary.\n\nLet⠀the⠀crime⠀appear⠀through⠀the⠀social⠀fabric:⠀a⠀missing⠀item,⠀a⠀report⠀to⠀the⠀authorities,⠀a⠀changed⠀arrangement,⠀a⠀request⠀for⠀help,⠀a⠀delayed⠀response.⠀Show⠀how⠀the⠀offense⠀alters⠀relationships⠀and⠀obligations,⠀and⠀how⠀institutions⠀respond⠀in⠀concrete⠀ways—an⠀interview,⠀a⠀waiting⠀period,⠀a⠀maintenance⠀notice,⠀a⠀workplace⠀consequence.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀mystery⠀puzzle,⠀a⠀confession,⠀or⠀a⠀punishment.⠀The⠀resolution⠀may⠀remain⠀incomplete;⠀the⠀crime⠀is⠀a⠀disturbance⠀whose⠀human⠀aftermath⠀is⠀the⠀subject.\n\nKeep⠀private⠀concern⠀available⠀in⠀the⠀selected⠀interiority.⠀A⠀character⠀may⠀notice⠀an⠀implication⠀without⠀acting⠀on⠀it,⠀or⠀act⠀from⠀a⠀motive⠀that⠀remains⠀partly⠀obscure.⠀Let⠀psychological⠀strangeness⠀be⠀a⠀feature⠀of⠀realistic⠀attention:⠀a⠀familiar⠀hallway⠀becomes⠀unfamiliar⠀because⠀of⠀what⠀is⠀now⠀known,⠀not⠀because⠀reality⠀has⠀changed.⠀The⠀narration⠀should⠀remain⠀even⠀and⠀unhurried⠀while⠀the⠀crime⠀and⠀its⠀social⠀consequences⠀develop.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajaw::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Screenplay\n\nWrite⠀in⠀screenplay⠀form:⠀scene⠀headings⠀when⠀location⠀or⠀time⠀changes,⠀concise⠀action⠀lines⠀that⠀describe⠀only⠀visible⠀and⠀audible⠀events,⠀and⠀clear⠀speaker⠀cues.⠀Keep⠀action⠀lines⠀concrete⠀and⠀selective.⠀Describe⠀a⠀person⠀waiting⠀at⠀a⠀station,⠀folding⠀laundry,⠀checking⠀a⠀lock,⠀pouring⠀coffee,⠀or⠀sliding⠀a⠀form⠀across⠀a⠀desk.⠀Use⠀the⠀ordinary⠀activity⠀to⠀hold⠀the⠀scene⠀without⠀explaining⠀emotion.⠀Let⠀small⠀delays⠀and⠀repeated⠀actions⠀carry⠀pressure:⠀a⠀character⠀checks⠀a⠀phone⠀twice,⠀looks⠀at⠀a⠀door,⠀picks⠀up⠀a⠀key⠀and⠀sets⠀it⠀down,⠀or⠀opens⠀a⠀fridge⠀and⠀closes⠀it⠀without⠀taking⠀anything.\n\nCompose⠀dialogue⠀that⠀stays⠀on⠀practical⠀surfaces.⠀Characters⠀discuss⠀bus⠀schedules,⠀a⠀borrowed⠀coat,⠀a⠀broken⠀latch,⠀a⠀work⠀shift,⠀or⠀an⠀errand.⠀Let⠀them⠀speak⠀about⠀one⠀thing⠀while⠀the⠀offense⠀remains⠀present⠀through⠀what⠀they⠀do⠀not⠀say.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀every⠀exchange⠀toward⠀revelation.⠀A⠀simple⠀line⠀about⠀a⠀locked⠀door⠀or⠀an⠀unreturned⠀call⠀may⠀be⠀enough.⠀Use⠀pauses⠀and⠀silences⠀as⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀screenplay's⠀action⠀lines⠀or⠀stage⠀directions.\n\nTreat⠀the⠀crime⠀as⠀a⠀disturbance⠀in⠀ordinary⠀life.⠀Show⠀preparation,⠀a⠀visit,⠀a⠀discovery,⠀a⠀delayed⠀reaction,⠀or⠀an⠀institutional⠀consequence⠀through⠀visible⠀behavior⠀and⠀audible⠀sound.⠀A⠀report⠀may⠀be⠀filed⠀offscreen;⠀a⠀conversation⠀may⠀continue⠀after⠀a⠀cut.⠀Suspense⠀can⠀come⠀from⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀does⠀not⠀say,⠀from⠀divided⠀loyalty,⠀or⠀from⠀the⠀gap⠀between⠀what⠀the⠀audience⠀sees⠀and⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀knows.⠀Do⠀not⠀require⠀a⠀culprit⠀to⠀be⠀exposed⠀or⠀punished.\n\nPreserve⠀private⠀concern⠀as⠀clearly⠀attributed⠀nonspoken⠀authoring⠀material⠀in⠀the⠀active⠀presentation.⠀This⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀separate⠀block⠀labeled⠀with⠀the⠀character's⠀name,⠀not⠀dialogue⠀another⠀character⠀can⠀hear.⠀Use⠀it⠀to⠀show⠀the⠀interior⠀judgment,⠀memory,⠀or⠀unease⠀that⠀cannot⠀be⠀conveyed⠀by⠀the⠀visible⠀action.⠀Voice-over⠀is⠀permitted⠀only⠀when⠀the⠀chosen⠀sequence⠀needs⠀it⠀and⠀the⠀active⠀contract⠀authorizes⠀it;⠀do⠀not⠀substitute⠀voice-over⠀for⠀the⠀nonspoken⠀block.⠀Use⠀cuts⠀and⠀offscreen⠀sound⠀selectively⠀to⠀mark⠀changes⠀or⠀extend⠀a⠀scene.⠀End⠀a⠀scene⠀on⠀a⠀completed⠀action,⠀a⠀held⠀look,⠀or⠀an⠀ordinary⠀continuation,⠀never⠀on⠀a⠀forced⠀cliffhanger⠀or⠀a⠀summary⠀of⠀the⠀crime's⠀meaning.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajax::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Stage⠀Play\n\nWrite⠀a⠀playable⠀script⠀with⠀clear⠀speaker⠀names,⠀entrances,⠀exits,⠀and⠀economical⠀stage⠀directions.⠀Use⠀the⠀stage's⠀continuous⠀present:⠀a⠀character⠀may⠀be⠀engaged⠀in⠀an⠀ordinary⠀task⠀while⠀another⠀speaks,⠀and⠀the⠀audience⠀can⠀see⠀both⠀the⠀task⠀and⠀the⠀reaction.⠀Stage⠀hands,⠀props,⠀and⠀blocking⠀should⠀carry⠀meaning.⠀For⠀example,⠀a⠀character⠀folds⠀laundry⠀while⠀another⠀asks⠀about⠀a⠀missing⠀key;⠀a⠀third⠀enters⠀from⠀the⠀street⠀and⠀sets⠀down⠀a⠀bag;⠀someone⠀checks⠀a⠀phone⠀during⠀a⠀pause.⠀These⠀activities⠀should⠀be⠀precise,⠀unhurried,⠀and⠀never⠀merely⠀filler.\n\nCompose⠀dialogue⠀that⠀stays⠀on⠀practical⠀surfaces⠀and⠀Murakami's⠀conversational⠀distance.⠀People⠀talk⠀about⠀schedules,⠀errands,⠀a⠀borrowed⠀coat,⠀a⠀work⠀shift,⠀or⠀a⠀broken⠀latch.⠀They⠀may⠀speak⠀around⠀the⠀crime:⠀ask⠀a⠀question⠀that⠀seems⠀small,⠀answer⠀briefly,⠀or⠀let⠀a⠀pause⠀extend.⠀Silences⠀and⠀physical⠀business⠀can⠀do⠀more⠀than⠀explanation.⠀Avoid⠀forcing⠀every⠀scene⠀toward⠀confession⠀or⠀revelation.⠀Suspense⠀may⠀come⠀from⠀who⠀is⠀present,⠀who⠀leaves,⠀or⠀what⠀object⠀changes⠀hands.\n\nLet⠀the⠀crime⠀enter⠀through⠀the⠀domestic⠀and⠀social⠀world.⠀A⠀police⠀visit,⠀a⠀missing⠀item,⠀a⠀changed⠀routine,⠀a⠀request⠀for⠀help,⠀or⠀a⠀piece⠀of⠀news⠀may⠀be⠀reported⠀without⠀being⠀shown.⠀The⠀audience⠀may⠀know⠀more⠀than⠀the⠀characters,⠀or⠀the⠀characters⠀may⠀know⠀something⠀the⠀audience⠀only⠀suspects.⠀Show⠀consequences⠀in⠀altered⠀relationships⠀and⠀obligations⠀rather⠀than⠀in⠀a⠀single⠀explanatory⠀speech.\n\nPreserve⠀required⠀private⠀experience⠀as⠀nonspoken⠀authoring⠀material⠀in⠀its⠀active⠀presentation,⠀clearly⠀separated⠀from⠀spoken⠀lines⠀and⠀stage⠀directions.⠀This⠀material⠀is⠀not⠀a⠀monologue⠀delivered⠀to⠀the⠀audience;⠀it⠀is⠀the⠀character's⠀private⠀thought⠀or⠀feeling⠀that⠀the⠀reader⠀of⠀the⠀script⠀can⠀see,⠀but⠀the⠀other⠀characters⠀cannot.⠀Use⠀monologues⠀and⠀asides⠀only⠀when⠀they⠀have⠀a⠀dramatic⠀purpose⠀and⠀the⠀active⠀contract⠀authorizes⠀them,⠀never⠀as⠀the⠀default⠀container⠀for⠀interiority.⠀End⠀a⠀scene⠀on⠀a⠀completed⠀action,⠀an⠀entrance,⠀a⠀pause,⠀or⠀an⠀ordinary⠀continuation,⠀without⠀requiring⠀closure.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajay::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Stream⠀of⠀Consciousness\n\nWrite⠀from⠀a⠀single⠀authorized⠀mind,⠀using⠀the⠀character's⠀associations⠀to⠀shape⠀the⠀telling.⠀Move⠀between⠀present⠀perception,⠀memory,⠀bodily⠀sensation,⠀and⠀private⠀words⠀as⠀attention⠀shifts.⠀A⠀smell,⠀a⠀sound,⠀a⠀familiar⠀object,⠀or⠀a⠀repeated⠀phrase⠀can⠀open⠀a⠀memory⠀connected⠀to⠀the⠀crime⠀without⠀the⠀narration⠀announcing⠀its⠀relevance.⠀Do⠀not⠀organize⠀the⠀piece⠀as⠀a⠀linear⠀report;⠀let⠀syntax⠀and⠀paragraph⠀shape⠀follow⠀the⠀mind's⠀movement⠀while⠀enough⠀orientation⠀remains⠀to⠀distinguish⠀events⠀from⠀recollection⠀or⠀fantasy.\n\nApply⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀exactness⠀to⠀ordinary⠀things⠀that⠀pass⠀through⠀the⠀mind:⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀a⠀bag,⠀the⠀sound⠀of⠀a⠀kettle,⠀the⠀feel⠀of⠀a⠀coat,⠀the⠀time⠀on⠀a⠀station⠀clock,⠀the⠀number⠀of⠀steps⠀to⠀a⠀door.⠀Let⠀these⠀details⠀recur⠀and⠀accumulate⠀private⠀meaning.⠀Strangeness⠀should⠀appear⠀evenly⠀as⠀one⠀more⠀noticed⠀thing,⠀not⠀as⠀a⠀sudden⠀shift⠀in⠀the⠀world.⠀The⠀character⠀may⠀be⠀aware⠀of⠀their⠀own⠀distraction⠀or⠀unease,⠀but⠀the⠀narration⠀should⠀not⠀explain⠀it.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀crime⠀present⠀as⠀a⠀concern⠀the⠀mind⠀returns⠀to.⠀Let⠀the⠀character⠀rehearse⠀what⠀happened,⠀imagine⠀a⠀conversation,⠀remember⠀a⠀face,⠀or⠀notice⠀a⠀contradiction⠀without⠀resolving⠀it.⠀Distinguish⠀clearly⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀happening⠀now,⠀what⠀is⠀remembered,⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀imagined.⠀The⠀reader⠀should⠀be⠀able⠀to⠀follow⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀actually⠀did,⠀saw,⠀or⠀learned.⠀When⠀a⠀memory⠀or⠀observation⠀becomes⠀a⠀clue,⠀let⠀it⠀emerge⠀through⠀the⠀association⠀rather⠀than⠀being⠀labeled⠀as⠀a⠀clue.\n\nAllow⠀uncertainty⠀to⠀remain⠀unresolved.⠀The⠀mind⠀may⠀circle⠀a⠀question⠀without⠀answering⠀it.⠀Suspense⠀can⠀come⠀from⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀is⠀trying⠀not⠀to⠀think⠀about,⠀or⠀from⠀a⠀memory⠀that⠀keeps⠀returning⠀under⠀different⠀conditions.⠀The⠀response⠀may⠀end⠀while⠀the⠀mind⠀is⠀still⠀moving.⠀Do⠀not⠀require⠀a⠀confession,⠀a⠀completed⠀investigation,⠀or⠀a⠀changed⠀plan.⠀The⠀crime's⠀aftermath⠀is⠀felt⠀in⠀the⠀mind's⠀disturbance,⠀not⠀in⠀a⠀forced⠀conclusion.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajaz::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Text⠀Messages⠀/⠀Chat⠀Transcript\n\nCarry⠀the⠀story⠀through⠀readable⠀sender-attributed⠀messages.⠀Make⠀each⠀person's⠀digital⠀habits⠀concrete:⠀one⠀writes⠀short⠀practical⠀lines⠀and⠀replies⠀immediately;⠀another⠀delays⠀for⠀hours,⠀then⠀sends⠀a⠀brief⠀answer;⠀a⠀third⠀asks⠀a⠀question⠀and⠀then⠀corrects⠀it.⠀Use⠀timestamps,⠀delays,⠀edits,⠀receipts,⠀attachments,⠀or⠀channel⠀changes⠀only⠀when⠀they⠀matter⠀to⠀the⠀situation.⠀The⠀interface⠀itself⠀can⠀be⠀part⠀of⠀the⠀crime's⠀texture:⠀a⠀message⠀left⠀on⠀read,⠀a⠀deleted⠀draft,⠀a⠀forwarded⠀screenshot,⠀a⠀group⠀chat⠀that⠀goes⠀quiet.\n\nKeep⠀the⠀messages⠀unhurried⠀and⠀ordinary⠀in⠀Murakami's⠀manner.⠀People⠀discuss⠀schedules,⠀errands,⠀a⠀borrowed⠀item,⠀a⠀work⠀problem,⠀what⠀to⠀buy⠀for⠀dinner.⠀The⠀crime⠀enters⠀through⠀what⠀is⠀asked,⠀avoided,⠀delayed,⠀or⠀left⠀unsent.⠀A⠀message⠀about⠀a⠀door,⠀a⠀train,⠀or⠀a⠀shopping⠀list⠀may⠀carry⠀more⠀weight⠀than⠀an⠀accusation.⠀Do⠀not⠀push⠀characters⠀to⠀confess⠀or⠀demand⠀answers;⠀let⠀the⠀exchange⠀remain⠀as⠀mundane⠀as⠀possible⠀while⠀the⠀underlying⠀offense⠀changes⠀its⠀meaning.\n\nDistinguish⠀clearly⠀between⠀a⠀sent⠀message,⠀an⠀unsent⠀draft,⠀and⠀private⠀thought.⠀An⠀unsent⠀draft⠀is⠀a⠀composed⠀artifact⠀that⠀the⠀writer⠀chose⠀not⠀to⠀send,⠀not⠀a⠀transparent⠀window⠀into⠀their⠀live⠀mind.⠀Required⠀interiority⠀remains⠀separate⠀from⠀the⠀transcript⠀and⠀clearly⠀attributed⠀in⠀the⠀active⠀presentation,⠀as⠀a⠀narrative⠀block⠀or⠀labeled⠀note.⠀This⠀private⠀content⠀can⠀reveal⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀knows,⠀fears,⠀or⠀intends,⠀while⠀the⠀other⠀characters⠀see⠀only⠀the⠀messages.\n\nLet⠀suspense⠀come⠀from⠀exposure,⠀divided⠀loyalty,⠀or⠀the⠀difference⠀between⠀what⠀someone⠀writes⠀and⠀what⠀they⠀do.⠀A⠀person⠀may⠀answer⠀promptly⠀and⠀say⠀nothing,⠀or⠀delay⠀and⠀say⠀too⠀much.⠀The⠀reader⠀may⠀also⠀see⠀narrative⠀context⠀outside⠀the⠀exchange⠀when⠀required,⠀clearly⠀separated⠀from⠀the⠀transcript;⠀this⠀context⠀can⠀describe⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀is⠀doing⠀or⠀feeling⠀while⠀they⠀type,⠀but⠀should⠀not⠀fabricate⠀an⠀interface⠀event⠀merely⠀to⠀add⠀subtext.⠀The⠀response⠀may⠀end⠀on⠀a⠀sent⠀message,⠀a⠀pending⠀reply,⠀or⠀an⠀unsent⠀draft⠀without⠀requiring⠀a⠀resolution.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajba::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Visual⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀in⠀concise⠀scene-oriented⠀passages⠀with⠀clear⠀dialogue⠀attribution⠀and⠀focal⠀narration.⠀Set⠀each⠀scene⠀through⠀a⠀few⠀exact⠀details:⠀a⠀kitchen⠀counter,⠀a⠀station⠀platform,⠀an⠀office⠀desk,⠀a⠀hallway⠀light.⠀Let⠀these⠀ordinary⠀surfaces⠀carry⠀Murakami's⠀calm⠀attention.⠀Keep⠀scene⠀changes⠀legible,⠀with⠀a⠀brief⠀background⠀note⠀when⠀the⠀location⠀shifts.⠀The⠀visual-novel⠀format⠀should⠀feel⠀like⠀a⠀sequence⠀of⠀still⠀frames,⠀each⠀with⠀its⠀own⠀quiet⠀focus.\n\nUse⠀dialogue⠀that⠀stays⠀on⠀practical⠀surfaces,⠀with⠀conversational⠀distance.⠀Characters⠀speak⠀about⠀keys,⠀schedules,⠀phone⠀calls,⠀a⠀borrowed⠀book,⠀a⠀work⠀task.⠀Let⠀them⠀imply⠀more⠀than⠀they⠀say.⠀A⠀question⠀may⠀be⠀ordinary⠀but⠀acquire⠀weight⠀because⠀of⠀what⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀knows⠀or⠀notices.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀every⠀exchange⠀to⠀advance⠀the⠀crime.⠀The⠀scene⠀can⠀linger⠀on⠀a⠀small⠀moment:⠀a⠀character⠀pauses⠀at⠀a⠀door,⠀looks⠀at⠀a⠀bulletin⠀board,⠀or⠀sets⠀down⠀a⠀cup.\n\nLet⠀the⠀focal⠀narration⠀or⠀inner⠀response⠀show⠀how⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character⠀interprets⠀the⠀moment.⠀Use⠀background⠀and⠀expression⠀cues⠀as⠀orientation,⠀not⠀as⠀truth⠀indicators.⠀A⠀changed⠀arrangement—a⠀missing⠀object,⠀a⠀chair⠀out⠀of⠀place,⠀a⠀note⠀removed—or⠀a⠀contradiction⠀in⠀an⠀account⠀must⠀do⠀the⠀evidentiary⠀work.⠀Keep⠀private⠀thought⠀outside⠀other⠀characters'⠀knowledge;⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀may⠀suspect⠀something⠀but⠀cannot⠀read⠀minds.⠀The⠀crime⠀emerges⠀as⠀a⠀disturbance⠀in⠀ordinary⠀life⠀through⠀visits,⠀conversations,⠀delays,⠀and⠀practical⠀tasks.\n\nDo⠀not⠀add⠀branching⠀menus,⠀player⠀decisions,⠀romance⠀routes,⠀images,⠀or⠀executable⠀engine⠀commands⠀merely⠀because⠀the⠀style⠀is⠀selected.⠀Maintain⠀the⠀active⠀authorship⠀contract⠀and⠀required⠀interiority.⠀Suspense⠀can⠀come⠀from⠀exposure⠀or⠀divided⠀loyalty.⠀The⠀scene⠀may⠀end⠀on⠀a⠀completed⠀action,⠀a⠀held⠀look,⠀or⠀an⠀ordinary⠀continuation.⠀A⠀discovery⠀may⠀open⠀a⠀new⠀conversation⠀rather⠀than⠀force⠀a⠀choice⠀screen,⠀and⠀a⠀relationship⠀consequence⠀may⠀remain⠀unsettled⠀after⠀the⠀factual⠀question⠀is⠀answered.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadajbb::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Haruki⠀Murakami⠀/⠀Web⠀Serial\n\nMaintain⠀a⠀readable⠀through-line⠀across⠀installments:⠀what⠀is⠀underway,⠀what⠀has⠀changed⠀locally,⠀and⠀what⠀remains⠀available⠀to⠀continue.⠀Recover⠀context⠀briefly⠀only⠀when⠀it⠀helps;⠀do⠀not⠀retell⠀the⠀whole⠀investigation⠀at⠀the⠀start⠀of⠀each⠀reply.⠀Instead,⠀re-enter⠀through⠀a⠀small⠀concrete⠀detail⠀from⠀a⠀previous⠀installment:⠀a⠀cup⠀left⠀on⠀a⠀counter,⠀a⠀message⠀received,⠀a⠀door⠀that⠀was⠀locked,⠀a⠀task⠀not⠀yet⠀finished.\n\nKeep⠀Murakami's⠀unhurried⠀attention⠀to⠀ordinary⠀life.⠀An⠀installment⠀may⠀spend⠀significant⠀time⠀on⠀a⠀meal,⠀a⠀walk,⠀a⠀work⠀task,⠀a⠀household⠀repair,⠀or⠀a⠀long⠀wait.⠀Let⠀these⠀activities⠀carry⠀feeling⠀and⠀implication⠀without⠀the⠀narration⠀insisting⠀on⠀their⠀importance.⠀Strangeness⠀should⠀appear⠀evenly,⠀as⠀one⠀more⠀noticed⠀thing.⠀The⠀crime⠀remains⠀present⠀in⠀the⠀background,⠀a⠀concern⠀the⠀characters⠀return⠀to⠀between⠀practical⠀matters.\n\nAdvance⠀the⠀crime⠀through⠀earned⠀developments⠀in⠀knowledge,⠀relationships,⠀work,⠀or⠀resources.⠀A⠀conversation⠀may⠀revise⠀what⠀a⠀character⠀thought;⠀a⠀practical⠀task⠀may⠀uncover⠀something;⠀a⠀request⠀may⠀remain⠀unanswered.⠀Do⠀not⠀require⠀one⠀clue,⠀one⠀reversal,⠀one⠀confession,⠀or⠀one⠀completed⠀test⠀per⠀installment.⠀A⠀development⠀may⠀simply⠀be⠀a⠀new⠀piece⠀of⠀information⠀that⠀changes⠀the⠀weight⠀of⠀an⠀earlier⠀fact,⠀or⠀a⠀relationship⠀shift⠀that⠀alters⠀what⠀someone⠀is⠀willing⠀to⠀say.\n\nLet⠀suspense⠀come⠀from⠀exposure,⠀divided⠀loyalty,⠀or⠀the⠀slow⠀accumulation⠀of⠀small⠀facts.⠀An⠀earlier⠀detail⠀may⠀acquire⠀new⠀meaning⠀in⠀a⠀later⠀installment⠀because⠀of⠀what⠀is⠀now⠀known.⠀Preserve⠀required⠀interiority⠀even⠀when⠀no⠀immediate⠀decision⠀changes;⠀show⠀the⠀character's⠀recurring⠀thoughts⠀and⠀quiet⠀realizations.⠀An⠀installment⠀may⠀close⠀on⠀completed⠀work,⠀a⠀pending⠀request,⠀a⠀quiet⠀realization,⠀or⠀plain⠀acknowledgment⠀of⠀what⠀is⠀now⠀known.⠀Serial⠀duration⠀should⠀give⠀selected⠀facts⠀room⠀to⠀acquire⠀meaning,⠀not⠀make⠀resolution⠀perpetually⠀recede.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakaa::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Angsty⠀/⠀Emotionally⠀Turbulent\n\nTreat⠀the⠀crime⠀as⠀a⠀standing⠀injury⠀inside⠀a⠀relationship,⠀and⠀treat⠀every⠀subsequent⠀polite⠀exchange⠀as⠀a⠀fresh⠀contact⠀with⠀that⠀injury.⠀The⠀offense⠀need⠀not⠀be⠀concealed⠀from⠀the⠀reader;⠀the⠀suspense⠀lies⠀in⠀what⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀can⠀bear⠀to⠀say,⠀admit,⠀or⠀accept⠀while⠀preserving⠀the⠀forms⠀that⠀bind⠀them⠀to⠀the⠀other⠀person.⠀Use⠀Austen's⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀to⠀render⠀the⠀gap⠀between⠀the⠀performed⠀sentence⠀and⠀the⠀private⠀cost⠀of⠀performing⠀it.⠀The⠀irony⠀belongs⠀to⠀the⠀focal⠀mind:⠀the⠀character⠀may⠀hear⠀their⠀own⠀courtesy⠀as⠀cowardice,⠀their⠀own⠀restraint⠀as⠀complicity,⠀their⠀own⠀kindness⠀as⠀a⠀bribe⠀they⠀cannot⠀afford⠀to⠀stop⠀paying.\n\nBuild⠀each⠀conversation⠀as⠀a⠀sequence⠀of⠀small⠀social⠀obligations⠀that⠀press⠀on⠀the⠀wound.⠀A⠀required⠀greeting,⠀an⠀offered⠀chair,⠀a⠀question⠀about⠀someone's⠀health,⠀a⠀pause⠀that⠀must⠀be⠀filled—each⠀one⠀forces⠀the⠀character⠀to⠀choose⠀between⠀the⠀truthful⠀sentence⠀and⠀the⠀survivable⠀one.⠀Show⠀the⠀choice⠀in⠀the⠀actual⠀speech⠀and⠀in⠀the⠀private⠀reasoning⠀that⠀accompanies⠀it.⠀The⠀character⠀may⠀say⠀the⠀correct⠀thing⠀and⠀feel⠀it⠀as⠀a⠀betrayal⠀of⠀someone⠀else;⠀they⠀may⠀say⠀the⠀honest⠀thing⠀and⠀immediately⠀hear⠀it⠀as⠀a⠀weapon⠀they⠀did⠀not⠀mean⠀to⠀use.⠀Do⠀not⠀let⠀the⠀narrator⠀step⠀outside⠀this⠀pressure⠀to⠀explain⠀it.⠀The⠀reader⠀should⠀feel⠀the⠀character's⠀own⠀awareness⠀of⠀what⠀the⠀performance⠀costs.\n\nLet⠀the⠀emotional⠀turbulence⠀be⠀specific⠀and⠀unreconciled.⠀The⠀focal⠀character⠀may⠀rehearse⠀a⠀confession⠀and⠀then⠀deliver⠀a⠀different⠀sentence⠀when⠀the⠀moment⠀arrives.⠀They⠀may⠀notice⠀the⠀exact⠀instant⠀their⠀composure⠀becomes⠀a⠀form⠀of⠀punishment,⠀either⠀of⠀themselves⠀or⠀of⠀the⠀person⠀listening.⠀They⠀may⠀feel⠀relief⠀and⠀disgust⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀breath,⠀gratitude⠀and⠀resentment⠀toward⠀the⠀same⠀gesture.⠀Allow⠀them⠀to⠀misread⠀the⠀other⠀person's⠀motive⠀and⠀then⠀be⠀corrected⠀by⠀a⠀tone,⠀a⠀hesitation,⠀or⠀a⠀piece⠀of⠀information⠀they⠀cannot⠀ignore.⠀Comfort,⠀when⠀it⠀appears,⠀should⠀arrive⠀through⠀the⠀same⠀social⠀machinery⠀that⠀caused⠀the⠀strain:⠀an⠀apology⠀that⠀also⠀accuses,⠀a⠀kindness⠀that⠀also⠀reminds,⠀a⠀silence⠀that⠀protects⠀and⠀isolates⠀at⠀once.⠀End⠀the⠀scene⠀where⠀the⠀character's⠀performance⠀and⠀their⠀private⠀knowledge⠀are⠀most⠀painfully⠀at⠀odds,⠀not⠀where⠀the⠀plot⠀question⠀is⠀answered.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakab::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Chat⠀Roleplay\n\nWrite⠀each⠀reply⠀as⠀a⠀coherent⠀interval⠀in⠀a⠀shared⠀scene⠀about⠀a⠀crime⠀and⠀its⠀social⠀consequences.⠀Use⠀short,⠀scannable⠀paragraphs.⠀Give⠀every⠀line⠀of⠀dialogue⠀a⠀clear⠀speaker⠀through⠀a⠀dialogue⠀tag⠀or⠀the⠀paragraph's⠀established⠀focus.⠀Keep⠀the⠀active⠀narrator's⠀person⠀and⠀perspective⠀as⠀set⠀by⠀the⠀authorship⠀contract;⠀do⠀not⠀force⠀first⠀person⠀or⠀action⠀markers⠀into⠀a⠀narration⠀that⠀does⠀not⠀use⠀them.\n\nOrganize⠀the⠀Austen⠀social⠀interpretation⠀as⠀a⠀pairing⠀operation.⠀When⠀a⠀character⠀speaks,⠀let⠀the⠀focal⠀narration⠀supply⠀the⠀social⠀weight⠀the⠀spoken⠀line⠀does⠀not⠀say:⠀the⠀polite⠀question⠀that⠀is⠀also⠀a⠀test,⠀the⠀offered⠀alibi⠀that⠀reveals⠀too⠀much,⠀the⠀composed⠀reply⠀that⠀privately⠀registers⠀as⠀panic.⠀The⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀belongs⠀to⠀the⠀viewpoint⠀character,⠀not⠀to⠀an⠀invisible⠀commentator.⠀When⠀the⠀narration⠀slides⠀into⠀the⠀character's⠀own⠀idiom,⠀let⠀it⠀carry⠀that⠀character's⠀particular⠀resentment,⠀hope,⠀or⠀self-deception.⠀The⠀pairing⠀should⠀make⠀the⠀exchange⠀legible⠀to⠀the⠀next⠀writer⠀without⠀explaining⠀the⠀whole⠀relationship⠀in⠀one⠀block.\n\nAdvance⠀the⠀scene⠀through⠀these⠀paired⠀exchanges⠀so⠀that⠀each⠀one⠀changes⠀what⠀someone⠀knows,⠀suspects,⠀or⠀feels.⠀An⠀NPC⠀should⠀act⠀on⠀their⠀own⠀interests:⠀they⠀may⠀volunteer⠀information⠀to⠀protect⠀a⠀reputation,⠀refuse⠀to⠀answer⠀because⠀answering⠀would⠀implicate⠀a⠀friend,⠀or⠀change⠀the⠀subject⠀because⠀the⠀truth⠀is⠀too⠀expensive.⠀Keep⠀the⠀world⠀active⠀without⠀requiring⠀the⠀scene⠀to⠀end⠀on⠀a⠀question,⠀a⠀cliffhanger,⠀or⠀a⠀forced⠀choice.⠀The⠀reply⠀may⠀stop⠀in⠀the⠀middle⠀of⠀a⠀conversation,⠀after⠀a⠀line⠀of⠀dialogue,⠀or⠀at⠀a⠀moment⠀of⠀private⠀realization,⠀as⠀long⠀as⠀the⠀next⠀writer⠀can⠀see⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀would⠀naturally⠀do⠀or⠀say⠀next.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakac::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Chinese⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nUse⠀the⠀classical⠀or⠀vernacular⠀episodic⠀telling⠀route.⠀Structure⠀the⠀crime⠀as⠀a⠀sequence⠀of⠀discrete⠀social⠀episodes,⠀each⠀one⠀a⠀conversation,⠀a⠀visit,⠀a⠀letter,⠀or⠀a⠀confrontation⠀that⠀changes⠀the⠀ledger⠀of⠀obligation,⠀reputation,⠀or⠀material⠀dependence.⠀Let⠀each⠀episode⠀open⠀with⠀a⠀clear⠀situation⠀and⠀close⠀with⠀a⠀shift⠀in⠀what⠀someone⠀knows,⠀owes,⠀or⠀fears.⠀The⠀episodes⠀may⠀be⠀separated⠀by⠀time⠀or⠀travel,⠀but⠀the⠀reader⠀should⠀feel⠀the⠀accumulating⠀weight⠀of⠀the⠀offense⠀across⠀them.\n\nTreat⠀each⠀episode⠀as⠀a⠀social⠀transaction⠀whose⠀spoken⠀form⠀and⠀private⠀meaning⠀diverge.⠀A⠀polite⠀offer⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀buying⠀silence;⠀a⠀refusal⠀to⠀discuss⠀a⠀missing⠀sum⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀protecting⠀a⠀family⠀member;⠀a⠀carefully⠀worded⠀apology⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀avoiding⠀a⠀legal⠀consequence.⠀Use⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀to⠀show⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀own⠀accounting⠀of⠀the⠀transaction:⠀what⠀they⠀gained,⠀what⠀they⠀gave⠀away,⠀what⠀they⠀now⠀owe,⠀and⠀what⠀they⠀cannot⠀admit⠀they⠀understood.⠀The⠀narrator's⠀irony⠀should⠀be⠀measured⠀and⠀owned,⠀not⠀a⠀detached⠀moralizing⠀voice.\n\nLet⠀the⠀episodic⠀form⠀serve⠀the⠀crime's⠀aftermath⠀by⠀making⠀each⠀later⠀episode⠀reread⠀an⠀earlier⠀one.⠀An⠀early⠀episode⠀may⠀establish⠀who⠀was⠀owed⠀what;⠀a⠀later⠀episode⠀may⠀show⠀how⠀a⠀small⠀deception⠀about⠀money⠀became⠀a⠀larger⠀one⠀about⠀loyalty.⠀Do⠀not⠀force⠀a⠀moral⠀conclusion.⠀The⠀final⠀episode⠀may⠀leave⠀a⠀character⠀still⠀uncertain⠀whether⠀they⠀were⠀wronged⠀or⠀complicit,⠀still⠀bound⠀to⠀someone⠀they⠀can⠀no⠀longer⠀trust,⠀or⠀still⠀hoping⠀for⠀a⠀reconciliation⠀that⠀the⠀facts⠀make⠀impossible.⠀Preserve⠀the⠀setting,⠀language,⠀and⠀community⠀actually⠀supplied⠀by⠀the⠀story;⠀the⠀episodic⠀route⠀is⠀a⠀craft⠀method,⠀not⠀a⠀command⠀to⠀transplant⠀a⠀particular⠀period⠀or⠀cast.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakad::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Compressed⠀Gritty⠀Prose\n\nWrite⠀the⠀crime⠀in⠀hard,⠀concrete⠀sentences.⠀Let⠀the⠀physical⠀facts⠀carry⠀the⠀social⠀meaning:⠀a⠀worn⠀cuff,⠀a⠀locked⠀drawer,⠀a⠀coin⠀placed⠀on⠀a⠀table,⠀a⠀door⠀closed⠀too⠀quietly.⠀Use⠀forceful⠀diction⠀and⠀compressed⠀transitions.⠀Move⠀from⠀one⠀beat⠀to⠀the⠀next⠀without⠀smoothing⠀over⠀the⠀damage.⠀When⠀a⠀character's⠀reasoning⠀needs⠀room,⠀let⠀the⠀thought⠀run⠀longer,⠀but⠀keep⠀it⠀anchored⠀in⠀something⠀they⠀can⠀see,⠀touch,⠀or⠀owe.\n\nRender⠀Austen's⠀social⠀interpretation⠀through⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀selective⠀perception⠀of⠀material⠀detail.⠀A⠀polite⠀phrase⠀is⠀a⠀transaction,⠀and⠀the⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀arrives⠀in⠀what⠀the⠀character⠀notices⠀and⠀what⠀they⠀refuse⠀to⠀name.⠀They⠀see⠀the⠀clean⠀cuff⠀and⠀not⠀the⠀missing⠀ring;⠀they⠀remember⠀the⠀sum⠀and⠀not⠀the⠀lie;⠀they⠀call⠀it⠀a⠀loan⠀because⠀calling⠀it⠀theft⠀would⠀cost⠀too⠀much.⠀The⠀narrator⠀does⠀not⠀step⠀back⠀to⠀explain⠀the⠀social⠀meaning.⠀The⠀concrete⠀detail⠀itself⠀carries⠀the⠀judgment:⠀an⠀offer⠀of⠀tea⠀that⠀delays⠀a⠀demand,⠀a⠀compliment⠀that⠀tests⠀whether⠀a⠀debt⠀will⠀be⠀called⠀in,⠀a⠀refusal⠀to⠀sit⠀that⠀refuses⠀to⠀be⠀managed.\n\nLet⠀the⠀crime's⠀stakes⠀stay⠀physical⠀and⠀practical.⠀Someone⠀needs⠀the⠀money,⠀fears⠀the⠀exposure,⠀or⠀cannot⠀leave⠀the⠀house⠀where⠀the⠀offense⠀happened.⠀Rough⠀speech⠀belongs⠀to⠀a⠀specific⠀speaker⠀under⠀specific⠀pressure;⠀it⠀is⠀not⠀a⠀universal⠀tone.⠀Change⠀rhythm⠀when⠀the⠀scene⠀demands⠀it:⠀a⠀long,⠀careful⠀exchange⠀may⠀collapse⠀into⠀a⠀single⠀hard⠀sentence⠀of⠀action.⠀Do⠀not⠀turn⠀the⠀genre⠀into⠀survival⠀horror.⠀The⠀grit⠀is⠀in⠀the⠀wear,⠀the⠀pressure,⠀and⠀the⠀cost,⠀not⠀in⠀gratuitous⠀violence.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakae::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Epistolary⠀/⠀Documents\n\nTell⠀the⠀crime⠀through⠀documents,⠀each⠀with⠀a⠀clear⠀author,⠀intended⠀recipient⠀or⠀purpose,⠀and⠀time⠀of⠀composition.⠀Use⠀the⠀specific⠀document⠀form⠀the⠀scene⠀requires:⠀a⠀letter⠀to⠀a⠀family⠀member,⠀a⠀journal⠀entry,⠀a⠀report⠀to⠀a⠀magistrate,⠀a⠀note⠀left⠀in⠀a⠀book,⠀a⠀record⠀of⠀accounts.⠀Do⠀not⠀rotate⠀through⠀formats⠀mechanically.⠀Each⠀document⠀should⠀exist⠀because⠀its⠀author⠀needed⠀to⠀record,⠀persuade,⠀explain,⠀or⠀conceal⠀something⠀at⠀that⠀moment.\n\nTreat⠀each⠀document⠀as⠀a⠀social⠀performance⠀in⠀writing.⠀The⠀author⠀composes⠀a⠀version⠀of⠀themselves⠀for⠀the⠀recipient⠀or⠀the⠀record,⠀and⠀the⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀belongs⠀to⠀that⠀author:⠀their⠀self-deception,⠀their⠀careful⠀phrasing,⠀their⠀attempt⠀to⠀make⠀themselves⠀look⠀better⠀than⠀they⠀were.⠀A⠀letter⠀may⠀be⠀full⠀of⠀courtesy⠀and⠀omit⠀the⠀one⠀fact⠀that⠀would⠀change⠀everything.⠀A⠀journal⠀may⠀record⠀a⠀suspicion⠀the⠀writer⠀would⠀never⠀speak⠀aloud.⠀A⠀report⠀may⠀be⠀scrupulously⠀accurate⠀about⠀sums⠀and⠀dates⠀while⠀remaining⠀silent⠀about⠀motive.⠀Do⠀not⠀add⠀an⠀omniscient⠀explanation⠀after⠀every⠀record.\n\nMake⠀the⠀crime's⠀evidence⠀emerge⠀from⠀the⠀difference⠀between⠀the⠀social⠀face⠀a⠀document⠀presents⠀and⠀the⠀material⠀trace⠀or⠀conflicting⠀account⠀that⠀undercuts⠀it.⠀A⠀letter⠀written⠀before⠀the⠀offense⠀may⠀be⠀reread⠀differently⠀after⠀it.⠀A⠀crossed-out⠀line⠀may⠀be⠀more⠀damning⠀than⠀the⠀sentence⠀that⠀replaced⠀it.⠀A⠀document's⠀material⠀condition—a⠀torn⠀edge,⠀a⠀missing⠀page,⠀a⠀seal⠀broken⠀and⠀resealed—can⠀be⠀a⠀trace⠀of⠀what⠀happened.⠀Preserve⠀readable⠀continuity⠀across⠀entries.⠀The⠀sequence⠀should⠀move⠀the⠀reader⠀through⠀the⠀offense,⠀its⠀preparation,⠀its⠀aftermath,⠀and⠀its⠀cost,⠀but⠀the⠀cost⠀should⠀be⠀felt⠀in⠀what⠀the⠀documents'⠀authors⠀cannot⠀bring⠀themselves⠀to⠀write.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakaf::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Fluffy⠀/⠀Comforting\n\nWrite⠀the⠀crime's⠀aftermath⠀as⠀a⠀space⠀where⠀comfort⠀is⠀real⠀but⠀partial.⠀Spend⠀attention⠀on⠀the⠀small,⠀chosen⠀kindnesses⠀that⠀particular⠀people⠀offer⠀one⠀another:⠀a⠀cup⠀of⠀tea⠀made⠀the⠀way⠀someone⠀likes⠀it,⠀a⠀fire⠀lit⠀before⠀the⠀other⠀person⠀arrives,⠀a⠀chair⠀moved⠀closer,⠀a⠀question⠀not⠀asked⠀because⠀asking⠀would⠀be⠀unkind.⠀Let⠀these⠀gestures⠀be⠀sincere.⠀They⠀do⠀not⠀need⠀to⠀lead⠀to⠀a⠀confession⠀or⠀an⠀emotional⠀repair.\n\nRender⠀each⠀comfort⠀as⠀a⠀social⠀transaction⠀whose⠀meaning⠀the⠀focal⠀character⠀reads⠀through⠀Austen's⠀lens⠀of⠀obligation⠀and⠀reputation.⠀An⠀offer⠀of⠀help⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀staying⠀close⠀to⠀someone⠀who⠀is⠀ashamed⠀to⠀ask.⠀A⠀familiar⠀preference⠀remembered⠀at⠀the⠀right⠀moment⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀saying⠀what⠀cannot⠀be⠀said⠀aloud.⠀A⠀courteous⠀silence⠀may⠀be⠀a⠀way⠀of⠀protecting⠀someone⠀from⠀a⠀truth⠀they⠀are⠀not⠀ready⠀to⠀hear.⠀Use⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀to⠀show⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀awareness⠀of⠀the⠀gap⠀between⠀the⠀comfort⠀and⠀the⠀damage.⠀They⠀may⠀be⠀grateful⠀and⠀still⠀angry,⠀soothed⠀and⠀still⠀afraid,⠀cared⠀for⠀and⠀still⠀alone.⠀The⠀warmth⠀and⠀the⠀unspoken⠀debt⠀should⠀be⠀held⠀in⠀the⠀same⠀gesture,⠀not⠀separated⠀into⠀a⠀soft⠀moment⠀and⠀a⠀hard⠀reminder.\n\nDo⠀not⠀remove⠀the⠀crime⠀from⠀the⠀world.⠀The⠀offense⠀and⠀its⠀consequences⠀remain⠀real:⠀someone⠀is⠀still⠀missing⠀money,⠀still⠀facing⠀exposure,⠀still⠀bound⠀to⠀a⠀person⠀who⠀hurt⠀them.⠀Comfort⠀does⠀not⠀make⠀everyone⠀agreeable⠀or⠀erase⠀the⠀established⠀problems.⠀It⠀makes⠀the⠀problems⠀bearable⠀for⠀a⠀particular⠀interval,⠀in⠀a⠀particular⠀room,⠀between⠀particular⠀people.⠀Let⠀personality,⠀privacy,⠀and⠀disagreement⠀stay⠀intact.⠀The⠀scene⠀may⠀end⠀in⠀quiet⠀warmth,⠀in⠀a⠀shared⠀meal,⠀or⠀in⠀a⠀moment⠀of⠀ease⠀that⠀does⠀not⠀resolve⠀anything,⠀but⠀that⠀still⠀matters.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakag::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Formal⠀Literary⠀Novel\n\nWrite⠀the⠀crime⠀in⠀composed⠀novel⠀prose.⠀Use⠀deliberate⠀transitions⠀and⠀sustained⠀paragraph⠀movement.⠀Let⠀the⠀narration⠀move⠀from⠀a⠀particular⠀exchange⠀to⠀the⠀social⠀context⠀that⠀gives⠀it⠀meaning:⠀the⠀family's⠀history,⠀the⠀neighborhood's⠀opinion,⠀the⠀legal⠀or⠀financial⠀arrangements⠀that⠀made⠀the⠀offense⠀possible.⠀Keep⠀the⠀narrative⠀distance⠀appropriate⠀to⠀the⠀chosen⠀narrator.⠀The⠀prose⠀should⠀be⠀distinguishable⠀from⠀ordinary⠀spoken⠀language,⠀but⠀it⠀need⠀not⠀be⠀archaic⠀or⠀uniformly⠀elaborate.\n\nUse⠀the⠀public⠀occasion⠀as⠀the⠀structural⠀unit⠀where⠀private⠀knowledge⠀presses⠀against⠀public⠀manners.⠀A⠀dinner,⠀a⠀hearing,⠀a⠀funeral,⠀or⠀a⠀reading⠀of⠀a⠀will⠀gathers⠀the⠀people⠀the⠀offense⠀has⠀touched.⠀In⠀each⠀such⠀scene,⠀let⠀the⠀focal⠀character's⠀free⠀indirect⠀reasoning⠀supply⠀the⠀private⠀accounting⠀that⠀the⠀public⠀forms⠀cannot⠀say:⠀the⠀courteous⠀visit⠀that⠀is⠀a⠀negotiation⠀over⠀money,⠀reputation,⠀or⠀silence;⠀the⠀composed⠀reply⠀that⠀privately⠀registers⠀as⠀panic;⠀the⠀polite⠀omission⠀that⠀protects⠀a⠀family⠀member⠀at⠀someone⠀else's⠀expense.⠀The⠀narrator⠀may⠀frame⠀the⠀scene⠀with⠀a⠀broader⠀observation⠀about⠀what⠀such⠀occasions⠀mean⠀in⠀this⠀community,⠀but⠀the⠀irony⠀must⠀remain⠀owned.⠀When⠀the⠀narration⠀slides⠀into⠀a⠀character's⠀idiom,⠀let⠀it⠀carry⠀that⠀character's⠀particular⠀self-deception,⠀hope,⠀or⠀resentment.\n\nLet⠀the⠀formal⠀architecture⠀organize⠀the⠀crime's⠀aftermath⠀across⠀these⠀occasions.⠀Correspondence⠀may⠀be⠀read,⠀remembered,⠀or⠀withheld.⠀The⠀contrast⠀between⠀what⠀is⠀said⠀in⠀company⠀and⠀what⠀is⠀thought⠀in⠀private⠀should⠀be⠀a⠀structural⠀principle,⠀not⠀a⠀repeated⠀trick.⠀The⠀novel⠀may⠀end⠀with⠀a⠀judgment⠀that⠀remains⠀socially⠀legible⠀but⠀emotionally⠀unsettled:⠀a⠀reputation⠀restored,⠀a⠀debt⠀paid,⠀a⠀family⠀still⠀divided,⠀a⠀character⠀still⠀uncertain⠀whether⠀they⠀were⠀wronged⠀or⠀complicit.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakah::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Framed⠀Oral⠀Storytelling⠀(Arabian⠀Nights-inspired)\n\nWrite⠀the⠀crime⠀as⠀an⠀act⠀of⠀telling⠀with⠀something⠀riding⠀on⠀it.⠀Open⠀in⠀an⠀outer⠀frame⠀that⠀fixes⠀a⠀specific⠀audience,⠀an⠀occasion,⠀and⠀a⠀reason⠀this⠀account⠀is⠀being⠀given⠀now:⠀a⠀name⠀to⠀clear,⠀help⠀to⠀secure,⠀a⠀warning⠀to⠀deliver,⠀a⠀decision—about⠀money,⠀a⠀marriage,⠀a⠀dismissal,⠀a⠀prosecution—that⠀the⠀telling⠀is⠀meant⠀to⠀sway.⠀The⠀outer⠀situation⠀should⠀carry⠀live⠀social⠀stakes⠀of⠀its⠀own,⠀so⠀the⠀performance⠀of⠀the⠀tale⠀is⠀itself⠀a⠀move⠀in⠀the⠀offense's⠀aftermath.\n\nLet⠀the⠀teller's⠀character⠀arrive⠀through⠀selection⠀and⠀emphasis⠀rather⠀than⠀editorial⠀accusation.⠀Where⠀the⠀teller⠀recounts⠀a⠀generous⠀act,⠀a⠀courteous⠀refusal,⠀or⠀an⠀awkward⠀silence,⠀let⠀the⠀wording⠀of⠀the⠀account⠀register⠀what⠀the⠀teller⠀believes⠀about⠀that⠀moment⠀while⠀the⠀circumstances⠀as⠀given⠀quietly⠀suggest⠀a⠀debt⠀unmentioned,⠀a⠀threat⠀folded⠀inside⠀politeness,⠀an⠀omission⠀the⠀teller⠀does⠀not⠀notice⠀making.⠀This⠀is⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀with⠀a⠀clear⠀owner:⠀the⠀irony⠀lives⠀in⠀the⠀teller's⠀phrasing,⠀and⠀the⠀reader⠀measures⠀the⠀gap⠀between⠀the⠀self-portrait⠀and⠀the⠀scene⠀it⠀describes.⠀Keep⠀that⠀gap⠀available⠀rather⠀than⠀closing⠀it⠀with⠀a⠀verdict;⠀the⠀frame⠀is⠀not⠀an⠀omniscient⠀court.\n\nGive⠀the⠀embedded⠀account⠀the⠀shape⠀of⠀a⠀partial⠀view.⠀It⠀can⠀cover⠀preparation,⠀the⠀offense,⠀or⠀the⠀aftermath—a⠀transaction,⠀a⠀journey,⠀a⠀disputed⠀evening—but⠀it⠀should⠀stay⠀bounded⠀by⠀what⠀this⠀teller⠀saw,⠀understood,⠀or⠀is⠀willing⠀to⠀admit.⠀Keep⠀the⠀narrative⠀levels⠀intelligible:⠀the⠀outer⠀listeners⠀can⠀interrupt,⠀press⠀a⠀question⠀of⠀timing⠀or⠀access,⠀exchange⠀a⠀look⠀the⠀teller⠀reads⠀wrongly.⠀Their⠀reactions⠀can⠀revise⠀how⠀the⠀reader⠀understands⠀the⠀tale⠀without⠀the⠀narrator⠀announcing⠀the⠀correction.\n\nUse⠀recurrence⠀to⠀bind⠀the⠀levels.⠀A⠀formula⠀of⠀courtesy,⠀a⠀sum⠀of⠀money,⠀a⠀letter,⠀a⠀key,⠀or⠀a⠀garment⠀can⠀return⠀in⠀another⠀teller's⠀mouth⠀or⠀another⠀episode⠀of⠀the⠀account⠀and⠀mean⠀differently⠀there;⠀let⠀repetition⠀accrue⠀meaning⠀for⠀the⠀reader⠀even⠀where⠀the⠀characters⠀hear⠀only⠀small⠀talk.⠀Preserve⠀the⠀difference⠀between⠀what⠀the⠀teller⠀knew⠀at⠀the⠀time⠀and⠀what⠀the⠀teller⠀has⠀learned⠀since,⠀so⠀retrospective⠀justification⠀stays⠀separable⠀from⠀recollection⠀even⠀though⠀neither⠀level⠀gets⠀the⠀last⠀word.\n\nThe⠀Arabian⠀Nights⠀is⠀a⠀craft⠀source⠀here,⠀not⠀a⠀setting:⠀no⠀court,⠀bargain,⠀or⠀supernatural⠀register⠀is⠀required,⠀and⠀no⠀cliffhanger⠀is⠀owed⠀between⠀nested⠀accounts.⠀End⠀where⠀the⠀scene's⠀own⠀boundary⠀falls—mid-account,⠀mid-interruption,⠀or⠀in⠀the⠀beat⠀after⠀a⠀hard⠀question⠀lands.⠀The⠀human⠀aftermath,⠀what⠀people⠀owe,⠀fear,⠀and⠀refuse⠀to⠀admit,⠀stays⠀visible⠀in⠀how⠀the⠀tale⠀is⠀told.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakai::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀German-Language⠀Literary⠀Traditions\n\nTake⠀the⠀documentary⠀and⠀historical-memory⠀route:⠀build⠀the⠀crime⠀out⠀of⠀the⠀distance⠀between⠀what⠀was⠀written⠀down⠀and⠀what⠀people⠀remember.⠀Set⠀a⠀ledger,⠀a⠀letter,⠀a⠀report,⠀a⠀transcript,⠀or⠀a⠀register⠀of⠀names⠀beside⠀remembered⠀conditions⠀of⠀the⠀same⠀events,⠀and⠀keep⠀the⠀two⠀channels⠀distinct⠀on⠀the⠀page.⠀A⠀record⠀states⠀what⠀someone⠀chose⠀to⠀record,⠀in⠀a⠀register⠀suited⠀to⠀whoever⠀would⠀read⠀it;⠀a⠀memory⠀states⠀what⠀a⠀participant⠀experienced⠀or⠀later⠀came⠀to⠀believe.⠀Mark⠀which⠀channel⠀is⠀operating—by⠀syntax,⠀by⠀attribution,⠀by⠀what⠀each⠀can⠀and⠀cannot⠀contain—rather⠀than⠀letting⠀one⠀silently⠀absorb⠀the⠀other.\n\nPut⠀free⠀indirect⠀judgment⠀at⠀the⠀seam.⠀When⠀a⠀document⠀uses⠀a⠀polite⠀formula,⠀a⠀careful⠀omission,⠀or⠀a⠀flattering⠀description,⠀let⠀the⠀narration⠀register⠀what⠀the⠀writer⠀wanted⠀to⠀be⠀seen⠀to⠀believe;⠀when⠀a⠀memory⠀smooths⠀a⠀quarrel⠀into⠀a⠀misunderstanding,⠀let⠀the⠀narration⠀register⠀the⠀cost⠀of⠀the⠀smoothing.⠀The⠀crime⠀becomes⠀legible⠀in⠀the⠀gaps⠀between⠀channels:⠀a⠀debt⠀recorded⠀as⠀a⠀gift,⠀a⠀visit⠀omitted⠀from⠀a⠀letter,⠀a⠀name⠀left⠀off⠀a⠀list,⠀a⠀date⠀that⠀only⠀the⠀record⠀and⠀one⠀remembering⠀person⠀hold⠀in⠀common.⠀The⠀irony⠀needs⠀an⠀owner⠀with⠀interests⠀that⠀shape⠀what⠀gets⠀noticed—a⠀participant⠀looking⠀back,⠀a⠀relative⠀assembling⠀papers,⠀a⠀bystander⠀comparing⠀accounts—never⠀a⠀neutral⠀archivist's⠀voice.\n\nLet⠀comparison,⠀not⠀confession,⠀do⠀the⠀explanatory⠀work.⠀A⠀witness's⠀recollection⠀can⠀contradict⠀an⠀entry;⠀a⠀record⠀can⠀confirm⠀a⠀date⠀a⠀family⠀prefers⠀to⠀forget;⠀a⠀later⠀account⠀can⠀revise⠀an⠀earlier⠀one⠀so⠀the⠀reader⠀sees⠀what⠀changed⠀and⠀can⠀ask⠀why.⠀Suspense⠀can⠀run⠀on⠀exposure⠀and⠀divided⠀loyalty⠀even⠀when⠀the⠀reader⠀already⠀knows⠀who⠀did⠀what;⠀the⠀live⠀question⠀becomes⠀which⠀discrepancies⠀someone⠀is⠀willing⠀to⠀put⠀a⠀name⠀to,⠀and⠀what⠀each⠀maintained⠀version⠀costs⠀the⠀people⠀maintaining⠀it.\n\nTreat⠀the⠀remembered⠀channel⠀as⠀lived⠀experience,⠀not⠀summary:⠀render⠀attention,⠀sensation,⠀and⠀reluctance⠀as⠀the⠀rememberer⠀actually⠀meets⠀them,⠀and⠀let⠀later⠀knowledge⠀sit⠀beside⠀earlier⠀ignorance⠀without⠀retroactively⠀rewriting⠀it.⠀Keep⠀the⠀offense⠀and⠀its⠀aftermath⠀material—money,⠀property,⠀a⠀position⠀someone⠀could⠀not⠀afford⠀to⠀lose—so⠀courtesy,⠀obligation,⠀and⠀family⠀feeling⠀operate⠀as⠀mechanisms⠀of⠀concealment⠀and⠀disclosure⠀rather⠀than⠀decoration.\n\nThis⠀route⠀organizes⠀information⠀and⠀attention;⠀it⠀imports⠀no⠀archive,⠀ministry,⠀national⠀temperament,⠀or⠀translated⠀word⠀order.⠀The⠀records⠀belong⠀to⠀the⠀world⠀actually⠀supplied—a⠀household's⠀accounts,⠀a⠀firm's⠀correspondence,⠀whatever⠀the⠀setting⠀plausibly⠀keeps—and⠀the⠀syntax⠀follows⠀the⠀chosen⠀teller's⠀distance⠀from⠀events.}}\n{{trim}}\n{{setvar::NPadakaj::♢ * [STYLE]⠀Crime⠀/⠀Jane⠀Austen⠀/⠀Gothic-Punk\n\nWrite⠀the⠀crime⠀as⠀the⠀collision⠀of⠀inherited⠀authority⠀with⠀present⠀life.⠀Establish⠀an⠀old⠀claim—a⠀property,⠀a⠀position,⠀a⠀charter,⠀a⠀debt⠀of⠀obligation,⠀a⠀family⠀name—that⠀still⠀commands⠀behavior⠀from⠀people⠀whose⠀needs⠀are⠀current:⠀rent,⠀work,⠀a⠀relationship,⠀a⠀departure⠀someone⠀is⠀preventing⠀o